<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Blasco Núñez Vela</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1490–<a href="/years/1546">1546</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Blasco Núñez Vela was the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> to enforce the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-laws">New Laws of 1542</a>, which limited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/encomienda">encomiendas</a> held by the conquerors. His arrival in 1544 provoked a revolt of encomenderos under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-pizarro">Gonzalo Pizarro</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/audiencia">Audiencia</a> deposed him, and he was defeated and killed by Pizarro's forces at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-anaquito">Battle of Añaquito</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a> in January 1546.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/blasco-nunez-vela.jpg" alt="Blasco Núñez Vela" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nu%C3%B1ez_Vela1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
